erm value creation  for us as a corporation rather than just  for focusing on the short-term outcome  so whether it's esg net zero climate  change actually business now recognized  and that shifted in the last 12 months  that to deliver value for their own  business as well as for wider society  they need to focus on that as long as  alongside a short-term financial return  and is there evidence that this works  better for businesses  yeah i think there's a lot of evidence  around this i mean  a purpose is what holds companies  together and increasingly those are a  economic and social purpose people want  to do things that are economically  financially but also socially useful on  a big scale and the people who work for  the company want to be part of that  shared success very important that  you're the purpose and that's one of the  things that we've seen in the last  12 18 months i'm sure you've seen it in  lng as well is our people are looking to  us to say actually what is the  organization that i'm working for it's  not just about the salary i'm paying at  the end of the month actually i want to  feel a connection that my purpose  resonates with the corporate purpose and  that you stand for something that i  believe in and actually we're seeing a  lot of corporates and clients changing  those courses emotional engagement is  the highest it's ever been in my career  right now is that and particularly  driven by lots of young people who who  really want to ask you difficult  questions about you know why am i here  why are we doing this what's the overall  objective and if it's a short-term goal  that doesn't really resonate  particularly well with technology and  science are changing so fast now it's  creating unbelievable opportunities for  us all and so the number of deals is  going to get done is going to rise  tremendously because the raw material  money is the cheapest it's ever been for  you know several hundred years and  therefore that's incredibly cheap but  actually getting the other bits of the  ingredients that make things successful  around a deal is increasingly difficult  because things are changing so quickly  and you want to develop the the purpose  and fit the culture together and it's  not about you know simple transactions  anymore we we consider deals in a much  broader context nigel i want to talk  about vision we've touched on it briefly  about the long term versus the short  term how important is this what we're  trying to do is invest in assets  that actually reflect society and  actually people can look around and see  wow this is what i'm invested in i'm  invested in all of these exciting  startup businesses across 20 different  universities in the uk i'm investing in  assets that are transforming the center  of various towns and cities i'm  investing assets that are delivering  affordable housing for people right  across the uk and that links up with the  purpose that we have as an organization  as well so people can have that massive  emotional engagement and it's a  consistency and a consistency a bit like  sports teams not just in a very short  time period but year after year after  year after year well ken what do you  think is driving this more purposeful  approach to deal making is it the  shareholders past experience  you know  the time we're in  i think it's an acceleration we've seen  in the last 12 months i think it was  already there in 2019 pre-pandemic but  actually we've all realized as human  beings we live in a fragile society and  actually we need to do more to embrace  the outcomes we want in the future we  all want a cleaner greener fair more  equitable society historically we have  the view that the government do  education and business does employment  actually if you look at organizations  that employ as many people as we do in  the uk we've got an obligation to  upskill because the world is moving so  fast whether it's technology development  we you know the pandemic has been  tremendous in driving real change and  accelerating change in lots of different  areas i mean it's it's a horrible thing  to happen but it's driven many of us  closer together and identified the  problems you know health inequality is  such a big issue  but part of the solution is for our  firms to step up our efforts in this all  the solutions are there it's about  people collaborating together to deliver  those  solutions and that's about teamwork  and you know going back to the sporting  analogy it's it's multi-disciplinary  teamwork you know the physios have to be  part of the team people in reception it  matters  what they like and how they greet people  when they when they come in the  professional standards that they set and  they themselves  want to move up the career ladder and  there's nothing  better and more motivating than people  within an organization having great peer  examples of people who've made  tremendous progress i think  collaboration is such a pertinent word  especially in sport because we've seen  how  you know managers the shareholders they  have to start listening to the fans  because fans now can galvanize they've  got social media they can put their  opinions out there and and if you don't  listen  they'll let you know not having fans at  matches has really made people realize  how important fans are yeah and how much  it impacts on the game when you don't  have the fans there it's been wonderful  to watch fans coming back and to feel  the atmosphere and to feel the lift you  get when you watch live sport with fans  there and it's very easy to dismiss fans  but you're only there because of them  you only exist  as a sports team because people want to  watch you and the minute they don't it's  all over the minute they stop buying the  shirts the minute they stop caring and i  think we they've been dismissed in the  past and that's that'll be a real change  that happens now there's been much more  thinking about how important fans are  from the club's point of view also we  have  fans rising up against  um team management making kind of  decisions to move off into the uh the  super league and i think  that was a real moment wasn't it when  you saw the fans  really feeling very strongly and feeling  empowered to express how they felt and  then the the withdraw the climb down  from that okay let's talk about the  importance of data how are businesses  using data to  evaluate their acquisition targets the  reality now is we live in a world that's  awash with data data is tracking our  everyday movements and actually  increasingly in evaluating acquisition  targets for our clients we're looking at  a whole range of data whether it's  customer engagement sentiment analysis  from the internet employee engagement  understanding their r d and innovation  pipeline because actually that alongside  the financial results you put those data  sets together and everything else that's  out there you can get a much more better  picture of  future performance likely future  performances and use those data sets in  a way that determines how the business  will optimize its performance post deal  and continue to grow and accelerate and  improve employment prospects for those  that employees in the communities  operates in and what do you think nigel  you know are they vital you know do you  look at them in your business no  absolutely you know nps scores employee  engagement scores sit right at the heart  of the business because they're  reflecting things that really matter to  us as a firm and you know financial  performance is just a part of it  definitely the others feed into the  financial performance and so i totally  agree with what ken said now nigel i'm  going to come to you for the last  thought  will business remain committed to this  more purposeful approach even if there's  you know changes in the economy yes yes  yes and i think we saw the economy  changing and actually lots of businesses  stepped up and lots of people within  those businesses stepped up because  you've got the raw material the money  we've got the capability we understand  the technology and the science we can  put on the data analytics we can put all  of this together to deliver incredible  solutions for society and we as business  leaders want to do that and our people  want us to do it and there's a real  society societal need for do for doing  that well this has been a fascinating  discussion and i'd like to thank our  guests for sharing their insights and i  hope you found this as interesting as i  have

